--!strict
-- Sky Citadel chunk kit. docs/biomes/SKY_CITADEL.md is the art direction; the pieces
-- are generated by assets/source/worlds/sky_citadel/build_sky_citadel_kit.py.
--
-- A white futurist citadel broken into floating islands above the cloud deck.
-- 22 pieces (2026-09-22), each built from a different mix of five axes --
-- island shape, floor, edge, keel, landmark -- so no two read alike.
--
-- CONNECTION VOCABULARY -- decided before modelling, per CHUNK_AUTHORING.md
-- "Starting a different world". Deliberately disjoint from Verdant Valley's
-- PATH/WIDE; a test asserts the two sets never overlap.
--   SKYWAY  connective. A 40-stud bridge deck, walk plane at the origin.
--   ASCENT  arena-only. A 72-stud grand approach with glowing kerbs. Only
--           the two gate-courts offer one, so a gate-court precedes the arena
--           on every seed -- the same emergent rule as VV's Grove.
--
-- THE SHAPE OF A RUN. Four turning pieces (two each way), one crossroads, and
-- a SIDE pocket. ChunkCore now picks a seeded exit among several, so the
-- crossroads can go straight, left or right; with IncludeSide on, the lookout
-- hangs off a spare socket. Nothing on the critical path dead-ends: the vault
-- that used to be the side pocket is now a turn you pass through.
--
-- SUPPORTS is the scenario-compatibility gate (build spec §7.3): what can
-- HAPPEN on a piece, as opposed to what the piece IS. Derived per piece from
-- its own description rather than applied uniformly -- the Archive takes
-- puzzles and secrets, the Armory takes a mini-boss, the shattered span takes
-- traversal and an ambush and neither of the other two. A kit whose pieces all
-- accepted everything would make the metadata decoration.
--
-- Sockets: Facing is degrees, 0 = -Z (north), 90 = +X, 180 = +Z (south),
-- 270 = -X. Offsets are local to the piece, before rotation.
--
-- SIZE: 256 x 256 x 256 for EVERY piece, exact rather than nominal.
-- ChunkLoader sets mesh.Size = (SizeX, SizeY, SizeZ), so a mesh whose
-- bounding box differs is stretched, and a MeshPart pivots on its box centre.
-- The generator pins the box with four 0.3-stud edge pins at z = -96 and one
-- landmark per piece at +160. The walk plane therefore sits 32 studs BELOW
-- the box centre -- the number GroundOffsetY will need (STATUS.md, High).

local function socket(id: string, kind: string, x: number, z: number, facing: number)
	return { Id = id, Kind = kind, OffsetX = x, OffsetY = 0, OffsetZ = z, Facing = facing }
end

